<section class="prose article-body" aria-labelledby="analytics-privacy-title">
    <h2 id="analytics-privacy-title">Website analytics</h2>
    <p>If you choose “Accept analytics”, Google Analytics 4 measures visits to the public journal website and downloads of published PDFs. It uses cookies and browser information to measure readership. Advertising personalization and Google signals are disabled.</p>
    <p>Optional analytics does not load before your consent. Login, registration, contact forms, account dashboards, manuscript submissions, search results and signed-in visits are excluded. Form contents, account identifiers and arbitrary URL query parameters are not sent by this integration.</p>
    <p>Your choice is stored in this browser for six months. Select “Analytics preferences” on a public page to change it. Choosing “Necessary only” removes the journal’s analytics cookies and stops optional tracking. Browser settings and blocking tools may also prevent collection.</p>
    <p>Google processes analytics data as a service provider. Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="external noopener">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>. For journal privacy enquiries, <a href="{{ route('contact') }}">contact the editorial office</a>.</p>
</section>
